{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqe5sbyj4uq","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"[ingest-candidate] edge metadata back-compat rule: legacy events without judged field default judged true when weight positive","summary":"source_task=091a4bf1-b671-4ff9-854d-993775faa5ee/21\nwhy: Non-obvious invariant required to prevent the judging gate from silently flipping all pre-existing promoted edges back to unjudged on daemon restart, which would block every already-released task.\nIn graph-store.js loadGraph, legacy edge events that lack a `judged` field default to `judged:true` when weight>0 (i.e. the edge was written before the judging system was introduced). This prevents tagBlindEdges from treating old weight>0 promoted edges as unjudged candidates. The guard is: `judged: typeof raw.judged !== 'undefined' ? raw.judged : (raw.weight > 0 ? true : false)`. Without this rule a daemon restart after the edge-metadata persist feature would mark every old promoted edge as unverified and re-block all tasks whose context_deps were already approved.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T19:09:57.259Z","vec":[-0.0736953467130661,0.051879022270441055,-0.01837182603776455,0.05217558145523071,0.0909515917301178,-0.04015082120895386,0.023544520139694214,-0.01966504566371441,0.00004911660653306171,0.028031909838318825,0.006259090267121792,-0.026393139734864235,-0.04588095098733902,0.01122216135263443,-0.043684832751750946,0.040195032954216,0.10782671719789505,-0.0145138343796134,-0.07552911341190338,-0.04271811619400978,0.03726731985807419,-0.05074227973818779,0.006810302846133709,-0.0063409036956727505,-0.018837885931134224,-0.013561172410845757,-0.11212529242038727,0.008685356006026268,0.10017121583223343,-0.05925951153039932,0.025524577125906944,0.031074341386556625,-0.05425583943724632,-0.0006770985783077776,-0.025101661682128906,0.021853478625416756,-0.06440778821706772,-0.02648819051682949,-0.03726581484079361,0.0036624683998525143,0.05629291012883186,0.069877